data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":0,"function":{"arguments":"{\"kind\":\"problem_brief\",\"title\":\"Problem Brief: Animated Weather App\",\"content\":\"## In short\\n- A **weather app whose whole interface animates to match the weather** (windy, rainy, snowy, hot, and so on).\\n- Includes the **standard features**: current location, saved cities, °C/°F toggle, and comparing cities.\\n- Works in a **browser on desktop and phone**.\\n\\n## Problem statement\\nYou want a weather app where the look and motion of the screen itself tell you the weather, instead of a static grid of numbers and icons. Most weather apps feel the same and are flat to look at. You also want the standard features people expect: your location, saved cities, a unit toggle and a way to compare places.\\n\\n## Who is affected\\n- **People who check the weather regularly** and would enjoy an app that feels alive and shows conditions at a glance through its visuals.\\n\\n## What happens today\\nTypical weather apps show data in static cards with small icons. They work, but the weather is something you read rather than feel, and they are not memorable.\\n\\n## What a fix would be worth\\nA more engaging, glanceable app that people prefer to open. No money or time figures were given.\\n\\n## Success criteria\\n- Opening the app shows current weather for your location, and the background and motion visibly match the conditions (for example rain falls, snow drifts, wind moves things, heat shimmers).\\n- Different conditions look clearly different from one another.\\n- You can switch between °C and °F and the whole app updates.\\n- You can search for, save and remove cities, and they are still there next time you open the app.\\n- You can compare two or more saved cities side by side.\\n- It looks and works well on both a phone and a desktop screen.\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Standard content: current conditions, hourly and multi-day forecast, feels-like, wind, humidity.\\n- Real forecast data comes from a free weather service, no account needed for you.\\n- No sign-in; saved cities are stored for the browser or device you use.\\n- Animations respect a \\\"reduce motion\\\" setting for people who need it.\\n- Radar maps and weather alerts are not in the first version.\\n\\n## Open questions\\nNone.\\n\"}"}}]},"finish_reason":null}]}

